rieved October 23, 2020.\n114. ↑ \"On the Motion to Proceed (Motion to Proceed to Legislative Session)\". Congress.gov. October 23, 2020. Archived from the original on February 15, 2021. Retrieved October 23, 2020.\n115. ↑ \"On the Motion to Proceed (Motion to Proceed to Executive Session to Consider the Nomination of Amy Coney Barrett to be an Associate Justice of the Supreme Court of the United States)\". Congress.gov. October 23, 2020. Archived from the original on February 15, 2021. Retrieved October 23, 2020.\n116. ↑ \"On the Motion to Table (Motion to Table the Motion to Indefinitely Postpone the Barrett Nomination)\". Congress.gov. October 23, 2020. Archived from the original on February 15, 2021. Retrieved October 23, 2020.\n117. ↑ Mineiro, Megan (October 23, 2020). \"Senate Teed Up for Monday Vote to Confirm Barrett\". Courthouse News Service. Archived from the original on February 15, 2021. Retrieved October 24, 2020.\n118. 1 2 Rybicki, Elizabeth (April 4, 2019). \"Senate Consideration of Presidential Nominations: Committee and Floor Procedure\" (PDF). Congressional Research Service. Archived (PDF) from the original on February 15, 2021. Retrieved October 18, 2020.\n119. ↑ Pergram, Chad (October 17, 2020). \"Amy Coney Barrett: The likely confirmation schedule for the Supreme Court nominee\". Fox News. Archived from the original on February 15, 2021. Retrieved October 18, 2020.\n120. ↑ Heitshusen, Valerie (April 14, 2017). \"Senate Proceedings Establishing Majority Cloture for Supreme Court Nominations: In Brief\" (PDF). Congressional Research Service. Archived (PDF) from the original on February 15, 2021. Retrieved October 18, 2020.\n121. ↑ \"Senate Vote 222 - On the Cloture Motion\". Pro Publica. October 25, 2020. Archived from the original on February 15, 2021. Retrieved October 25, 2020.\n122. ↑ Estepa, Jessica; Kelly, Erin (October 5, 2018). \"Brett Kavanaugh confirmation: When will the Senate vote and how long will it take?\". *USA Today*. Archived fr